    Exercise JSON logging in the OpenSearch scenario.
    
    Without a job that sets openstack_logging_json, everything added by
    this series is code no gate runs.
    
    This turns it on in the prometheus-opensearch scenario rather than
    adding a scenario of its own. That scenario is the only one that
    enables central logging, so it is the only place where the whole
    pipeline is exercised -- a service writes JSON, Fluentd parses and
    renames it, and the result has to arrive in OpenSearch. Anywhere else
    would only demonstrate that Fluentd did not fall over. It also costs
    no additional CI capacity, which a dedicated scenario would, six jobs
    at a time across three distributions and their upgrades.
    
    The text format keeps its coverage, since it stays the default
    everywhere and every other job still runs check-logs.sh against it.
    The scenario's own file matcher already includes the Fluentd role, so
    the patch that adds the JSON path runs these jobs.
    
    Known gap: the service conversion patches touch role templates that
    are not in this scenario's file matcher, so they do not trigger these
    jobs themselves. They are one line each and the mechanism is proven by
    the earlier patches, but a conversion that went wrong would not be
    caught until something else ran the scenario.
    
    Prompt: Michael asked for the whole series, including a CI scenario,
    to be implemented before pushing anything publicly, so that the story
    could be reviewed end to end.
    
